.TH ESDM\-ES\-PKCS11 8 "2026-11-03" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-es\-pkcs11 \- serve the random number generator of a PKCS#11 token to the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-es\-pkcs11
.RB [ \-\-module
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-token_label
.IR LABEL ]
.RB [ \-\-pin_file
.IR PATH " | "
.B \-\-pin_credential
.IR NAME ]
.RI [ "provider options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-es\-pkcs11
reads the random number generator of a PKCS#11 token \- a smartcard, a USB
token, an HSM, or SoftHSM \- with
.B C_GenerateRandom
through libp11, and serves it as an external entropy source, which
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext
reads. The PKCS#11 module, vendor code, runs in this process with the
privileges the token needs, not in the ESDM.
.PP
It uses the first slot holding an initialized token with a random number
generator, of the configured label if one is given. A token that is missing,
pulled, or fails a read is looked for again on demand, at most every 5
seconds, the module loaded anew when its slots hold none. A token is tested on
binding and on every self test of the ESDM \- two reads that must differ \- and
one repeating its output is credited with nothing until it passes again. No
module or token is no reason not to serve: the ESDM credits nothing meanwhile.
.SH THE PIN
The PIN is never given on the command line, which every user reads in
.IR /proc ,
nor at build time. It is the one line of the file of
.BR \-\-pin_file ,
or of a systemd credential in
.IR $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY :
the one of
.BR \-\-pin_credential ,
else
.B pkcs11\-pin
if the daemon has it. A file that is empty, holds more than one line of up to
256 bytes or is no regular file is refused; one every user reads is warned
about. A command line that is wrong is reported without repeating it, as it
may hold a PIN by mistake.
.PP
The user logs in only if the token asks for it. A failed login wipes the PIN,
which is not tried again before the daemon is started anew \- each one uses up
a PIN retry of the token \- and the token is used without a login. The daemon
keeps itself out of core dumps and of
.BR ptrace (2).
.SH NAME, RATE AND STATUS
The source declares the name
.B PKCS#11
followed by the token label, if that makes a valid name, and the entropy rate
of the meson option
.B es_pkcs11_entropy_rate
\- see
.B \-\-name
and
.B \-\-entropy_rate
of
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3).
Its status names the
.BR module ,
.BR token_label ,
.BR token ,
.BR slot ,
.BR token_present ,
.BR logged_in ,
.B pin
.RB ( none ", " set ", " refused ),
.B repetition_test
.RB ( none ", " passed ", " failed )
and
.BR last_error ;
text a token reports is shown with what is no UTF-8 and control characters
replaced by \(aq?\(aq.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-module " \fIPATH\fR"
The PKCS#11 module, by default that of the meson option
.BR es_pkcs11_module_path ,
required if it names none.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-token_label " \fILABEL\fR"
The label of the token to use, by default that of the meson option
.BR es_pkcs11_token_label .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pin_file " \fIPATH\fR"
Read the PIN from
.IR PATH ,
not together with
.BR \-\-pin_credential .
.TP
.BI \-\-pin_credential " NAME"
Read the PIN from the systemd credential
.IR NAME ,
which has to be there.
.TP
.I provider options
.BR \-\-socket ,
by default
.IR /run/esdm\-es\-pkcs11/esdm\-es\-pkcs11.socket ,
and the others of
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3).
.SH SYSTEMD
.B esdm\-es\-pkcs11.service
runs the daemon as the system user
.B esdm\-es\-pkcs11
before
.BR esdm\-server.service ,
the PIN imported as the credential
.BR pkcs11\-pin .
Its head shows the drop-ins configuring the module and the token, and the ESDM:
.PP
.nf
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext /run/esdm\-es\-pkcs11/esdm\-es\-pkcs11.socket \\
	\-\-es_ext_uid esdm\-es\-pkcs11
.fi
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
softhsm2\-util \-\-init\-token \-\-free \-\-label my\-token \-\-so\-pin 1234 \-\-pin 5678
(umask 077; echo 5678 > /etc/esdm/pkcs11\-pin)
esdm\-es\-pkcs11 \-\-module /usr/lib/softhsm/libsofthsm2.so \\
	\-\-token_label my\-token \-\-pin_file /etc/esdm/pkcs11\-pin \\
	\-\-socket /run/esdm\-es\-pkcs11.socket
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext /run/esdm\-es\-pkcs11.socket
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-es\-pcsc (8),
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Theil <theil.markus@gmail.com>
